From: OpenWrt AX3000E port
Date: Mon Aug 24 2026
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_rproc: forward-declare struct device

qcom_get_ssr_subdev_name() takes a `struct device *` parameter but the
header never forward-declares (or includes) struct device, only
struct notifier_block. GCC treats the first appearance of the struct
name inside a parameter list as a local declaration scoped to that
prototype ("declared inside parameter list will not be visible
outside of this definition or declaration"), which is legal C but
warned on; with -Werror (as used by the mac80211 backports build)
this is a hard build failure. Never reached before because the
mac80211/coccinelle backports step failed earlier in the build.

--- a/include/linux/remoteproc/qcom_rproc.h
+++ b/include/linux/remoteproc/qcom_rproc.h
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 #define __QCOM_RPROC_H__

 struct notifier_block;
+struct device;

 #if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_QCOM_RPROC_COMMON)

